re haphazard and scattered  in the 2d culture  and then you know kim-1 levels again are  much much higher in lonza cells than  in the m31 rp text and again they kind  of you know  steady up uh as you go on with culture  and this is you know a very healthy  culture if you're not treating it with  anything  and we really aim to replicate what the  developers have published so on the  right you can see key data  from webinar all 2016 publication kidney  international  and what our collaborators did they not  only described the model they also  put this model to the test with respect  to its physiology so in the middle on  the right you see that they have looked  at  uh switch and vitamin d metabolism uh  with you know  addition of calcitriol and then also  adjustability of cytokine for 15  24 a1 when you actually switch the  vitamin d metabolism and at the bottom  they found that as they lower ph of  their perfusion media they actually see  an increase in ammonia generation  so we tried to replicate these key  elements of their publication plus we  also tested  polymax and v effects and that's those  are panels across the top and the middle  ones  and you can see that polymex and b was  toxic to rptex  in 2d in both lonzon m31 cells but him  31 cells were very resilient  to power mix and be in 3d system when  lonza cells really died off  in the 3g chip and  important point of biomarkers of injury  kim won you can see it go up very early  if you can collect enough refusate  in these models but as you can see with  lots of cells at 48 hours you see kim 1  is actually going down  and it's not because there's less  toxicity there's actually fewer to no  cells to generate quinoa and to shed  that  into the media but more important or  interesting findings were with vitamin d  metabolism we found that both him one  team 31 cells and monza cells induced  cytochrome before 50 24 a1  in 3d culture not in 2d culture when we  added calcitriol  but we did not see the change in  me